From: YassinTM <232429671+YassinTM@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 02:04:36 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] HID: magicmouse: make the Force Click device a mouse for
 BTN_RIGHT

Port of 8263151fd onto Aurora's force_input device: libinput ignores a
device with only BTN_RIGHT, so add BTN_LEFT and REL_X/REL_Y when the deep
click is mapped to a right click.
---
 drivers/hid/hid-magicmouse.c | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/hid/hid-magicmouse.c b/drivers/hid/hid-magicmouse.c
index e909a698a..04525241a 100644
--- a/drivers/hid/hid-magicmouse.c
+++ b/drivers/hid/hid-magicmouse.c
@@ -2199,6 +2199,16 @@ static void magicmouse_setup_force_input(struct magicmouse_sc *msc)
 	input->id.version = hdev->version;
 	input->dev.parent = &hdev->dev;
 	input_set_capability(input, EV_KEY, haptic_deep_keycode);
+	if (haptic_deep_keycode == BTN_RIGHT) {
+		/*
+		 * libinput ignores a lone BTN_RIGHT and drops a clickpad's own
+		 * right button, so make this look like a mouse to report the
+		 * deep click as a right click.
+		 */
+		input_set_capability(input, EV_KEY, BTN_LEFT);
+		input_set_capability(input, EV_REL, REL_X);
+		input_set_capability(input, EV_REL, REL_Y);
+	}
 
 	ret = input_register_device(input);
 	if (ret) {
-- 
